{"id": "EUVD-2026-71309", "enisaUuid": "cf2f624c-bec3-38db-87ba-825810511975", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfuse: fix missing barrier when checking io-uring readiness\n\nfuse_block_alloc() reads fch->initialized and then fch->io_uring.\nfch->io_uring is set before fch->initialized, ordered by the smp_wmb()\nin fuse_chan_set_intialized(), but fuse_block_alloc() has no matching\nread barrier between the two loads.\n\nThis may lead a CPU to observe fch->initialized=1 but fch->io_uring=0,\nand skip the check that blocks request allocation until the io-uring\nqueues are ready. This can reintroduce the lock-order inversion deadlock\nthat commit 3393ff964e0f prevents.\n\nAdd an smp_rmb() barrier to pair with the smp_wmb() in\nfuse_chan_set_initialized() to prevent this.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:55:13", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:44:53", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8974575898cd7a4c818088f102b2e7a0286d3302", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dd9c835709f4bb3e4256eea7573e4e6e18f956de", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/edb310bc27f0ad83e7fd558a3caf1a94ca511654"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-80859", "GHSA-66f3-f7p7-8q9g"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0e32bfdd-e0db-3429-a756-b30bad408b19", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "28d0a37d-609b-3ab7-9e0b-9fe0af1bd6bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3393ff964e0fa5def66570c54a4612bf9df06b76 <dd9c835709f4bb3e4256eea7573e4e6e18f956de"}, {"id": "4510bc72-da7d-3a8c-bc71-34b6df1b50c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3393ff964e0fa5def66570c54a4612bf9df06b76 <8974575898cd7a4c818088f102b2e7a0286d3302"}, {"id": "4fea4804-786b-34e0-a9e1-64ac62aabe35", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.51"}, {"id": "a2f2f2ff-f994-3e06-a40e-9f378ec16cce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14"}, {"id": "ae5273ed-1532-3e85-bde1-563285e19c54", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "dd357d5e-d674-3b6e-a904-a7fe6443755f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3393ff964e0fa5def66570c54a4612bf9df06b76 <edb310bc27f0ad83e7fd558a3caf1a94ca511654"}, {"id": "e1dc6f31-b8a9-38b6-bf66-e1041afe84e9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ead8c374-ef08-39a3-a1f0-b35784a2f5fa", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}